  "prefLabel": "Plc 1311.02 Definitions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1311.02 Definitions. For purposes of this part, the following definitions shall apply:\n\n(a) “Respondent” means the person against whom a disciplinary sanction is proposed to be imposed; and\n\n(b) “Sexual misconduct” means engaging in one or more of the following activities with respect to a current patient who is not a spouse or domestic partner:\n\n(1) Engaging in sexual relations, whether consensual or non-consensual;\n\n(2) Making verbal or physical sexual advances;\n\n(3) Using sexual language or phrases;\n\n(4) Requesting sexual favors; or\n\n(5) Engaging in physical contact of a sexual nature.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1300) #13701, eff 8-1-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1300.html"
